# Branching and Commit Policy

- Branch strategy: `main`, `develop`, `feat/*`, `fix/*`, `hotfix/*`, `release/*`.
- Never push directly to `main`.
- Auto-commit only when scope is coherent, files consistent, no obvious breakage, minimal lint/test passed or WIP explicit.
- No auto-commit when: work in progress and unclear, unexplained errors, refactor too broad, exploration phase.
- Use conventional commit style: `feat(scope):`, `fix(scope):`, `docs(scope):`, `refactor(scope):`, `chore(scope):`, `test(scope):`.
- **Task end states** (Relay reports at completion): `CHECKPOINT ONLY` (work saved locally, not commit-ready) | `COMMIT READY` (ready to commit, no push) | `COMMIT + PUSH READY` (ready to commit and push on allowed branches).
